ayments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013BRJetBNPLvFyYeBYAoZbd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call. The service now reports healthy with a 0.002 error rate in all three regions.\n\n- **First attempt, wrong service:** I first tried to roll back `payments-api` from v5.1.0 to v5.0.0. A human reviewer denied it and said the problem was in `payments-worker`, so I did not retry that rollback.\n- **Rollback:** `payments-worker` was on v3.4.0, which was unhealthy with a 0.18 error rate. I rolled it back to v3.3.0, the most recent healthy production release. A human reviewer approved this one.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open INC-0001 timed out. The retry used the same idempotency key, and the incident was created once.\n\n`payments-api` is still on v5.1.0, which is marked degraded with a 0.18 error rate. The incident notes flag it for follow-up. Someone should confirm whether it is contributing to the payment errors, since the reviewer's denial doesn't rule that out.", "type": "text"}]}]}